    {
      "abstract": "$\\phi/K^-$ (a) and $\\phi/\\Xi^-$ (b) ratio as a function of collision energy, $\\sqrt{s_{\\mathrm{NN}}}$. The solid black circles show the measurements presented here in 0-10\\% centrality bin, while empty markers in black or grey are used for data from various other energies and/or collision systems. The grey solid line represents a THERMUS calculation based on the Grand Canonical Ensemble (GCE) while the dotted lines depict calculations based on the Canonical Ensemble (CE) with different parameters of strangeness correlation radius ($r_c$). The green dashed line, green shaded band and the solid red line show transport model calculations from the public versions $\\mathrm{UrQMD}^{1}$, modified $\\mathrm{UrQMD}^{2}$ and SMASH, respectively.",
